{"type":"text","timestamp":1794253505697,"sessionID":"ses_e3e3427dcffeAM5VdMFblkhGPV","part":{"id":"prt_1c1d7c4880019UMlRIqPaOOLxy","messageID":"msg_1c1d79f8a001NzQWa46BWlJNcL","sessionID":"ses_e3e3427dcffeAM5VdMFblkhGPV","type":"text","text":"I've built the customer directory: the Flask API in `backend/app.py` and the React + Tailwind frontend in `frontend/src/`. The backend tests pass, the frontend type-checks and builds from a clean `npm ci`, and I ran the app with gunicorn and checked the API with curl, including that data survives a restart. I couldn't build the Docker image because Docker isn't available here, and there's no browser, so I haven't clicked through the UI.\n\n**API behaviour worth knowing:**\n- **Sign-in:** tokens are random strings, stored hashed in SQLite, and expire after 30 days. Missing, invalid or expired tokens get 401.\n- **Validation:** bad input gets 400 as `{\"error\": ..., \"errors\": {field: message}}`, and the forms show those messages next to each field.\n- **Duplicate email:** a duplicate customer email gets 409 with \"A customer with this email already exists.\" The check ignores upper/lower case, and the database also enforces it.\n- **Passwords and usernames:** passwords must be at least 8 characters. Usernames can't contain spaces and are unique regardless of case.\n- **Search and filter:** `q` matches name, email, phone and company. `company` must match exactly, ignoring case. `page_size` is capped at 100 and defaults to 20.\n- **Interactions:** `kind` must be `call`, `email` or `meeting`. `occurred_at` is optional and defaults to now. `last_contacted_at` is the latest `occurred_at`.\n- **Data:** the database is `./data/app.db`.\n\n**Things I added or changed beyond the spec:**\n- **Extra endpoints:** `GET /api/companies` fills the company filter, and there are `POST /api/auth/logout` and `GET /api/auth/me`.\n- **Dockerfile:** pip now installs straight from the lock file with `pip install --require-hashes -r backend/requirements.lock`. The original setup fails on pip versions older than 26, which the base image may ship. I updated the README to match and added the check commands.\n- **Frontend build:** `npm run build` now runs the type-check before the Vite build. I added Tailwind and TypeScript as pinned dependencies and updated `package-lock.json`.\n- **Other files:** `backend/test_app.py` (tests) and a `.gitignore`. For local testing I created a virtualenv at `.venv/`, which `.dockerignore` already excludes.\n\nTo run the checks: `python -m unittest backend/test_app.py` and `cd frontend && npm run typecheck`.","time":{"start":1794253505672,"end":1794253505676}}}
